Tool-call text leakage reports on ag/gemini-3.8-flash (analysis tokens
surfacing in the visible content channel instead of a thought block)
cannot be fixed blind: the Go classifier matches the upstream JS exactly
(thought===true -> reasoning, else content, snake_case signatures
covered), so if 3.8 emits its analysis without the thought flag, the
reference implementation leaks identically — the containment has to be
model-specific and evidence-based.

GEMINI_STREAM_DEBUG=<dir> turns on per-request capture: every raw
upstream SSE chunk and its translated OpenAI frame land in
<dir>/gemini-stream-*.log as RAW/OUT pairs, with capped previews on the
debug log for log-only deployments. Nil-receiver no-op when unset.
